      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T17:52:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In particular `SkSharedMutex` eventually bottoms out in `sem_wait` which in G3 appears to have fiber support. On the other hand `std::shared_mutex` probably does not. It would be good to know if this is a restriction we\u0027re going to need to live with going forward (no use of `barrier`, `condition_variable`, `future`, `jthread`, `latch`, `mutex`, `shared_mutex`, `semaphore`, `stop_token`, and `thread` standard library stuff, at least on any code that might end up in G3).",
      "parentUuid": "035cacd9_a88e3ee5",
      "revId": "97412af4f4eadaea8ea71bc5011fdb16a71d9ccb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
